  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/... \nBy the end of the of the week and heading into the weekend, most \nglobal ensembles continue to support the strengthening of the high \npressure, with H5 heights up to 600dam and the center of the \nanticyclone shifting to over northern AZ/southern UT. These heights \nare near or at the max of NAEFS percentile for climatology for this \ntime of year, which are quite frankly impressive. The peak of the \nextreme heat is expected to be Friday and Saturday, where the \nchances of Phoenix Sky Harbor at least tying the record high (116F) \nwill be 65% on Friday and 50% Saturday. As mentioned previously, an \nadditional widespread Extreme Heat Warning will be likely near the \nend of the workweek. Additionally, this setup will likely add more \nsubsidence over the area and subdue afternoon convection. Global \nensembles also show a slow downtrend in PWATs, falling under 1.5\" by \nThursday- Friday. So, this is not great for the prospects of seeing \nstorms push into the lower deserts. However, the NBM keeps slight \nPoPs focused in the AZ high terrain.",
